478
00:32:14.054 --> 00:32:15.462
Context and Problem.

479
00:32:15.742 --> 00:32:28.499
The orders primary (Ch 10's quorum-sync cluster) is at 70 % CPU and 6.8 TB at P90 sale peaks, and projected to hit its write ceiling in ~9 months.

480
00:32:28.779 --> 00:32:35.201
A mod-N reshard in another team moved 80 % of its data and lost writes (§1.1).

481
00:32:35.481 --> 00:32:39.385
The store dashboard's storeid queries are the top CPU consumer.

482
00:32:39.665 --> 00:32:40.369
2.

483
00:32:40.649 --> 00:32:41.993
Goals or Non-Goals.

484
00:32:43.343 --> 00:32:58.639
Goals: scale writes and storage horizontally; keep checkout (order + items + payment) a local transaction; add shards online with no lost writes; per-customer and by-id reads on one shard; store queries without scatter-gather.

485
00:32:58.919 --> 00:33:07.708
Non-goals: cross-shard ACID transactions (Ch 13 sagas where needed); multi-region write placement (Ch 27).

