00:35:30.925 --> 00:35:31.693
5.

538
00:35:31.973 --> 00:35:41.807
Proposed design. bucket = CRC32C(customerid) mod 1024, in a shared library with golden-value tests.

539
00:35:42.087 --> 00:35:47.421
The function never changes. shardmap(bucket, shard, version) in the config DB.

540
00:35:47.701 --> 00:35:51.626
Pods poll every 5 s and reload immediately on BUCKETMOVED.

541
00:35:51.906 --> 00:35:53.677
Map versions only increase.

542
00:35:53.957 --> 00:36:05.135
Order ids carry the bucket (ordbucket hexms hexrandom), so by-id routing needs no lookup. orders, orderitems, payments and the outbox are co-located by bucket.

543
00:36:05.415 --> 00:36:08.829
Every table has bucket as the first primary-key column.

544
00:36:10.179 --> 00:36:14.253
Each shard is a Ch 10 cluster (quorum sync to 2 standbys).

545
00:36:14.533 --> 00:36:22.021
Store queries use ordersbystore, keyed by (storeid, salt), fed by order.order.placed.v1 and status events.

546
00:36:22.301 --> 00:36:24.477
Known hot stores get 4 to 8 salts.

547
00:36:24.757 --> 00:36:38.432
Moves: the bucket-mover job runs bulk copy, then catch-up (logical replication or change sequence), then fence (trigger on bucketfence), then final delta, then checksum, then map flip, then delayed delete.

548
00:36:38.712 --> 00:36:41.656
One bucket at a time per shard pair, rate-limited.

549
00:36:41.936 --> 00:36:49.637
Scatter-gather only for admin or support endpoints: per-shard limit, 300 ms deadline, partial results flagged.

550
